# hui DARK FORCE STYLE — the NATIVE-COMPARABLE rig (14z-69). Runs
# UNCHANGED on native vsav2 and on a variant-id build, so ours-vs-native
# is one diff at the same phase.
#
# ACTIVATING DARK FORCE FOR REAL (read this before editing the script —
# it is what the first version of this replay got wrong):
#   * DF is P+K of the SAME STRENGTH and **consumes one banked stock**.
#     With an empty meter the pair is DOWNGRADED to a single button and
#     the match continues normally: the tell is +0x109 (banked stock)
#     staying 0 and +0x107 reading 0xFF/0xFE. seq 0x0A is that
#     downgrade, NOT Dark Force.
#   * REAL DF is seq **0x16** (activation) settling to seq **0x18**, with
#     +0x109 DECREMENTED and +0x110/+0x111/+0x17B latched to 1 — the
#     fields vs2's own DF handler head-clears.
#   * On screen: the DF-specific background and the cyan TIME bar under
#     the health bar. If the stage looks ordinary, you are not in DF.
# So the runner MUST poke stocks in. POKES for both legs:
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03;3100:ff8509:03;3120:ff8509:03"
#   P1 $FF8782 = 0x10 (Huitzil, native id on both games)
#   P2 $FF8B82 = 0x03 (Victor — id 0x03 on vsav AND vsav2, verified by
#                      pick; without it the cursor path R,R lands on
#                      different characters on the two wheels and the
#                      sprite lists are not comparable)
#   P1 $FF8509 = 3 banked stocks (the documented ES-scripting poke,
#                docs/game/atlas/ram.md +0x109) so the pair is not downgraded
#
# THE BLOCKER THAT WAS NOT ONE: 14z-68j recorded "the early-window id
# poke does NOT force him on vsav2". That was replay 61, whose input
# timing is authored for OUR wheel. The replay-80 early-window poke flow
# DOES reach him natively — no vs2 cursor path and no savestate needed.
#
# WHY AIR DASH AND WALK: the maintainer's repro is "1 stock, HP+HK, then
# move — air dash shows it best", and the afterimages/recolour appear
# right at activation whenever he MOVES. Both motions are in this rig.
#
# THE CONTROL IS INSIDE THE REPLAY: the same air dash is performed before
# DF (f3160) and twice during it (f3520, f3620), so the mode's own
# contribution is visible without trusting two runs to line up.
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# control air dash, DF NOT yet active (replay 79 timing: jump f3160 is
# the measured-good accept frame; f3060 jumps are eaten on both games)
3160-3162 p1=U
3175-3177 p1=R
3181-3183 p1=R
# activate Dark Force: HP+HK, with the stocks poked in at f3100/f3120
3260-3263 p1=36
# DF walk (activation animation runs ~100f; he is actionable well before
# this)
3380-3480 p1=R
# DF air dash #1
3520-3522 p1=U
3535-3537 p1=R
3541-3543 p1=R
# DF air dash #2
3620-3622 p1=U
3635-3637 p1=R
3641-3643 p1=R
3800 wait
